# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root .gitignore
#
# server/.gitignore already covers the same ground for the server
# folder, but git only applies a nested .gitignore to its OWN folder
# and below. If you ever run "git init" HERE (at the project root),
# these rules are the ones that protect you. Keeping both means the
# secrets stay out of git no matter where the repo starts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Real secrets: JWT signing key and OpenAI API key.
# Only .env.example belongs in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
server/.env
server/.env.*
!server/.env.example

# The SQLite database — real accounts and bcrypt password hashes.
server/data/
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Installed packages — "npm install" recreates them.
node_modules/
server/node_modules/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
